WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.787
Unit 1 is automated investigation
and response, set per device group.

2
00:00:04.787 --> 00:00:07.312
Microsoft Learn lists five levels.

3
00:00:07.312 --> 00:00:10.225
Full, remediate threats automatically.

4
00:00:10.225 --> 00:00:14.080
Three semi levels, requiring
approval for core folders,

5
00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:16.762
for non-temp folders, or for all folders.

6
00:00:16.762 --> 00:00:18.612
And no automated response.

7
00:00:18.612 --> 00:00:21.863
The program's choices are
risk-based recommendations.

8
00:00:21.863 --> 00:00:26.599
The pilot puts ring one's workstation
group at semi, require approval for all

9
00:00:26.599 --> 00:00:29.456
folders, so every
remediation is proposed and

10
00:00:29.456 --> 00:00:32.163
an analyst approves it
in the Action center.

11
00:00:32.163 --> 00:00:34.358
Those two weeks of pending actions,

12
00:00:34.358 --> 00:00:37.613
with the approval rate
recorded, are the audit phase.

13
00:00:37.613 --> 00:00:41.062
Then workstation groups go to
full, which Learn recommends.

14
00:00:41.062 --> 00:00:43.275
Server groups stay at a semi level,

15
00:00:43.275 --> 00:00:47.937
because isolating a server is never
autonomous in the program's ladder.

16
00:00:47.937 --> 00:00:51.239
Rollback sets a device
group back to a semi level,

17
00:00:51.239 --> 00:00:56.438
on the Devices page under automated
responses in the Defender X D R settings.

18
00:00:56.438 --> 00:00:58.814
Learn says changing device groups needs

19
00:00:58.814 --> 00:01:01.800
Global Administrator or
Security Administrator.
